  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Why mid = low + (high - low) / 2",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "low and high are plain `int` indices",
            "Their **sum** can exceed the int limit",
            "The sum silently ==wraps== to a negative",
            "mid then points outside the array"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Both forms give the ==same midpoint==. Only the safe one never builds a value larger than `high`."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "2. Integer Limits",
          "items": [
            "`int` max = ==2,147,483,647==",
            "`long` max ≈ 9.2 x 10^18",
            "Java / C++ **wrap**, they do not warn"
          ],
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "java",
          "lines": [
            "int low  = 1000000000;",
            "int high = 2000000000;",
            "int mid = (low + high) / 2;",
            "// sum = 3e9 > int max",
            "// wraps to -1294967296",
            "// mid = -647483648 (bad!)"
          ],
          "note": "sum overflows before the divide"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "3. Expression",
            "Value",
            "Fits int?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "low + high",
              "3,000,000,000",
              "**No**, wraps"
            ],
            [
              "(low+high)/2",
              "-647,483,648",
              "wrong index"
            ],
            [
              "high - low",
              "1,000,000,000",
              "Yes"
            ],
            [
              "low + (high-low)/2",
              "1,500,000,000",
              "==Yes=="
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. The Safe Formula",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "java",
          "lines": [
            "int gap = high - low; // >= 0",
            "int mid = low + gap / 2;",
            "// gap <= high, never overflows",
            "// low + gap/2 <= high, safe"
          ],
          "note": "never builds the huge sum"
        },
        {
